==Jagex Launcher Improvements==
===New RuneLite Installations===
Today introduces further improvements to the Jagex Launcher, with seamless installation of the popular community led third-party client, RuneLite! 

We’ve improved the way new RuneLite users can install the client via the Launcher. Before today, you’d have had to click on “Install” and head to the RuneLite website to install the client. Now however, it is a simple case of selecting RuneLite as your preferred client within the Launcher, clicking “Play”, and the Launcher will automatically install the client for you and then load it. 

You might have to wait a few moments for the installer to finish, signalled by the “Play” button changing to a progress wheel. 

For many of you reading this post, you won’t notice a change, this only applies to those who do not currently have RuneLite installed. It is also possible to continue installing RuneLite directly from their site <u>[https://runelite.net/ https://runelite.net/]</u>.

==Other Changes==
We previously announced that the Easter 2026 Event would be removed today. However, the Easter Bunny hasn’t packed up the stalls and decorations just yet! You now have an extra week to go egg hunting before the event wraps up next Wednesday.

Now, onto the other changes of the week:

* Brutus icon now appears in HiScores interface on the Official Client.
* Some grammar has been corrected in the canoe experts' axe-related dialogue.
* The warning before climbing down the ladder from the Seers' Village rooftop course is now only shown if you're in the middle of the course at the time.

